{"qid": "b05", "family": "b", "split": "dev", "method": "M3", "model": "glm", "answer": {"method": "M3", "model": "glm", "final": {"answer": "According to the Rosemount 3051 datasheet (rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001, p. 77), the Rosemount 3051CFC_C Compact Orifice Flow Meter with Conditioning Option C, Ranges 2–3, with a beta ratio of 0.50 has a flow reference accuracy of ±1.95% of flow rate at 8:1 flow turndown. This applies to the FT-15-3 flow transmitter shown on the P&ID.", "not_present": false}, "outcome": "ANSWERED", "route": ["context_rag+chunks"], "cypher": [], "sources": [{"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "pages": [77, 43, 53, 105, 29, 28, 106, 104, 98, 45, 78, 57]}], "latency_s": 2.772999000037089, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 57043, "completion_tokens": 173, "cost_usd": 0.00170827, "spent_usd": 0.00170827, "n_calls": 2, "n_cached": 0, "models": ["qwen/qwen3-embedding-8b", "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash"]}, "trace": {"chunks": [{"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 77, "score": 0.7643}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 43, "score": 0.7432}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 53, "score": 0.7074}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 105, "score": 0.7073}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 29, "score": 0.6893}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 28, "score": 0.6582}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 106, "score": 0.6315}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 104, "score": 0.6304}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 98, "score": 0.6266}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 45, "score": 0.6259}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 78, "score": 0.6166}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 57, "score": 0.6163}], "prompt_chars": 143405, "reply": "{\"answer\": \"According to the Rosemount 3051 datasheet (rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001, p. 77), the Rosemount 3051CFC_C Compact Orifice Flow Meter with Conditioning Option C, Ranges 2–3, with a beta ratio of 0.50 has a flow reference accuracy of ±1.95% of flow rate at 8:1 flow turndown. This applies to the FT-15-3 flow transmitter shown on the P&ID.\", \"not_present\": false}"}}}
{"qid": "c01", "family": "c", "split": "dev", "method": "M3", "model": "glm", "answer": {"method": "M3", "model": "glm", "final": {"answer": "The transmitter feeding FIC-11-1 is FT-11-1, which is covered by the Rosemount 3051 datasheet (00813-0100-4001). On transmitter failure, the analog output is driven either high or low to alert the user; which direction applies is user-selectable with a jumper/switch on the transmitter. The actual alarm levels depend on the configuration: the default is NAMUR compliant (high alarm ≥ 21.75 mA, low alarm ≤ 3.75 mA), with Rosemount standard (high ≥ 22.5 mA, low ≤ 3.6 mA) and custom levels (high 20.2–23.0 mA, low 3.6–3.8 mA) also possible. The alarm direction/levels can be changed via the alarm levels option codes: C4 (NAMUR alarm high), CN (NAMUR alarm low), CR/CS (custom high/low, requires option code C1), or CT (Rosemount standard low alarm); these alarm-level options are only available with the HART 4–20 mA output (code A).", "not_present": false}, "outcome": "ANSWERED", "route": ["context_rag+chunks"], "cypher": [], "sources": [{"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "pages": [88, 109, 15, 46, 35, 86, 26, 74, 42, 83, 57, 63]}], "latency_s": 3.3015943999635056, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 57724, "completion_tokens": 339, "cost_usd": 0.00185483, "spent_usd": 0.00185483, "n_calls": 2, "n_cached": 0, "models": ["qwen/qwen3-embedding-8b", "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash"]}, "trace": {"chunks": [{"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 88, "score": 0.5973}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 109, "score": 0.5364}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 15, "score": 0.5356}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 46, "score": 0.521}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 35, "score": 0.5207}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 86, "score": 0.5187}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 26, "score": 0.5129}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 74, "score": 0.5118}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 42, "score": 0.5093}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 83, "score": 0.5092}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 57, "score": 0.5055}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 63, "score": 0.5008}], "prompt_chars": 146811, "reply": "{\"answer\": \"The transmitter feeding FIC-11-1 is FT-11-1, which is covered by the Rosemount 3051 datasheet (00813-0100-4001). On transmitter failure, the analog output is driven either high or low to alert the user; which direction applies is user-selectable with a jumper/switch on the transmitter. The actual alarm levels depend on the configuration: the default is NAMUR compliant (high alarm ≥ 21.75 mA, low alarm ≤ 3.75 mA), with Rosemount standard (high ≥ 22.5 mA, low ≤ 3.6 mA) and custom levels (high 20.2–23.0 mA, low 3.6–3.8 mA) also possible. The alarm direction/levels can be changed via the alarm levels option codes: C4 (NAMUR alarm high), CN (NAMUR alarm low), CR/CS (custom high/low, requires option code C1), or CT (Rosemount standard low alarm); these alarm-level options are only available with the HART 4–20 mA output (code A).\", \"not_present\": false}"}}}
